{
  "dom_id": "step-q105639",
  "name": "Question 2",
  "problem": "Calculate $∇\\cdot (3F+2G)$ for the vector fields $F$ and $G,$ where\n\n$$\nF={e}^{\\operatorname{sin}⁡x}\\,i+\\operatorname{cos}⁡({y}^{2})\\,j,\\,∇\\cdot G=3y\\operatorname{sin}⁡({y}^{2}).\n$$",
  "worked_solution": "If $F$ and $G$ are vector fields and $k$ is a constant, then we have the following  linearity properties for divergence:\n\n- $∇\\cdot (kF)=k∇\\cdot F$\n\n- $∇\\cdot (F+G)=∇\\cdot F+∇\\cdot G.$\n\nIn our case, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}∇\\cdot (3F+2G) & =∇\\cdot (3F)+∇\\cdot (2G) \\\\  & =3∇\\cdot F+2∇\\cdot G.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFirst, we need to calculate $∇\\cdot F.$ In doing so, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}∇\\cdot F & =\\frac{∂}{∂x}({e}^{\\operatorname{sin}⁡x})+\\frac{∂}{∂y}(\\operatorname{cos}⁡({y}^{2})) \\\\  & =\\operatorname{cos}⁡x{e}^{\\operatorname{sin}⁡x}-2y\\operatorname{sin}⁡({y}^{2}).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nApplying the linearity properties, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}∇\\cdot (3F+2G) & =3∇\\cdot F+2∇\\cdot G \\\\  & =3(\\operatorname{cos}⁡x{e}^{\\operatorname{sin}⁡x}-2y\\operatorname{sin}⁡({y}^{2}))+2\\cdot (3y\\operatorname{sin}⁡({y}^{2})) \\\\  & =3\\operatorname{cos}⁡x\\,{e}^{\\operatorname{sin}⁡x}-6y\\operatorname{sin}⁡({y}^{2})+6y\\operatorname{sin}⁡({y}^{2}) \\\\  & =3\\operatorname{cos}⁡x\\,{e}^{\\operatorname{sin}⁡x}.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
  "calculator_instructions": "",
